**Message 1 — What the problem is and what's changing**

> The two Azure AD variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_AZURE_CLIENT_ID` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_AZURE_TENANT_ID`) are currently baked into the Next.js build, so Kubernetes can't override them at runtime. The fix is to move them server-side. Instead of the browser reading them directly from the bundle, a small Next.js API route reads them on the server and hands them to the frontend at runtime. You'll rename the variables and add one new file.

