  tasks: [
    {
      title: "Save table edits permanently instead of losing them on refresh",
      category: "next_steps",
      description: `# Save table edits permanently instead of losing them on refresh

## What & Why
All Add / Edit / Delete operations on data tables currently only change a local copy in the browser (the UI shows an "Unsaved local changes" tag and a notice that "changes are saved locally until a backend write API is connected"). Users will lose every change on page refresh. To make CRUD real, the FastAPI backend needs write endpoints and the frontend needs to call them.

## Done looks like
- Backend (written as copy-paste instructions per project convention — no direct backend edits): new endpoints under api/v1/routes/tables.py, e.g. POST /v1/tables/{name} (insert row), PUT /v1/tables/{name}/{id} (update row), DELETE /v1/tables/{name}/{id} (delete row), and optionally column add/drop. Document them in docs/.
- Frontend: lib/api.ts gains createRow / updateRow / deleteRow helpers calling through the proxy with the Bearer token.
- components/DataTable.tsx: handleSave, handleDeleteRow, handleDeleteColumn call the API and refetch (or optimistically update) instead of only mutating localData; the "Unsaved local changes" dirty flag clears on successful persist.
- Errors are surfaced to the user (e.g. message.error) when a write fails.

## Relevant files
- \`lighthouse-frontend/components/DataTable.tsx\`
- \`lighthouse-frontend/lib/api.ts\`
- \`api/v1/routes/tables.py\` (instructions only)
- \`docs/\``
    }
  ]
});
